## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical cache invalidation design across multiple servers and cache backends, including stampedes, per-user invalidation, and pub/sub usage.

## Key Concepts
- Cache-aside pattern
- Per-user key naming and TTL
- Invalidation triggers for writes
- Distributed locks (SETNX/EX) to avoid stampede
- Pub/Sub advantages with Redis vs lack of notifications in Memcached

## Code Example
```javascript
async function getFeed(userId){
  const key = `feed:user:${userId}`
  const cached = await redis.get(key)
  if(cached) return JSON.parse(cached)
  const lock = `lock:feed:${userId}`
  if(await redis.set(lock, '1', 'NX', 'EX', 5)){
    const fresh = await computeFeed(userId)
    await redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(fresh), 'EX', 300)
    await redis.del(lock)
    return fresh
  } else {
    await sleep(50)
    return getFeed(userId)
  }
}

// Invalidation path (triggered by writes)
async function invalidateFeed(userId){
  const key = `feed:user:${userId}`
  await redis.del(key)
  if(usePubSub){
    await redis.publish(`feed-inval:${userId}`, 'invalidate')
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical OAuth2 debugging skills, understanding of token lifecycle, and real-world troubleshooting abilities that backend engineers face daily.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates identify: 1) Refresh token expired/revoked, 2) Scope mismatch between access and refresh tokens, 3) Client configuration issues. They should mention checking token introspection endpoint, reviewing logs, and testing with Postman/curl.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Debug refresh token failure
async function debugRefreshToken(refreshToken: string) {
  try {
    // 1. Check token introspection
    const introspect = await fetch('/oauth/introspect', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: `token=${refreshToken}`
    });

    // 2. Validate client configuration
    const clientConfig = await getClientConfig();

    // 3. Review token storage
    const storedToken = await getStoredToken(refreshToken);

    return { introspect, clientConfig, storedToken };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Debug failed:', error);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
